{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 2, :comments ["<b>The length of each curtain, eight and twenty cubits.</b> It is known that the making of the Tabernacle was entirely figured after the making of the heavens, and since the luminaries are fixed in the heavens and all actions come from there into the lower world at appointed times, therefore he used the term יריעה ('curtain') after the verse (Psalms 104:2): ״נוטה שמים כיריעה״. And there were ten curtains corresponding to the ten spheres, and he said 'eight and twenty' corresponding to the twenty-eight times in the book of Ecclesiastes, concerning which it is said (1 Chronicles 12:33): ״ומבני יששכר יודעי בינה לעתים״, and concerning them David said (Psalms 34:2): ״אברכה את ה' בכל עת״, and he further mentioned (ibid. 31:16): ״בידך עתותי״. Or it may correspond to the days of the moon's excess and diminution," "<b>And in the Midrash.</b> Tanhuma: eight and twenty cubits was the length of the curtain, and a great miracle — where do we find a single curtain of twenty-eight cubits? Rabbi Nehemiah says: it was a matter of miracles, created for the hour and then hidden away. <small>(See Tanhuma, and there the exposition concerns the curtains of goat hair, and the intention is regarding the covering of tachash skin, which was also thirty cubits long)</small>. You can know this, for it is written ״אורך היריעה האחת שלשים באמה״ — from where do you bring this? And you should not say this only of the curtains, but also of the boards there was a matter of miracles. End."], :book :exodus, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 26, :notes {1 "The phrase 'ולא תאמר ביריעות אלא אף בקרשים היה מעשה נסים' is rendered hyper-literally; the argument appears to be that just as the curtain dimensions involved miracle, so too the boards did, not that one should refrain from saying it of the curtains."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:04:38.531369689Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}